## 1. Friction Confirmation

**Distribution IS the #1 friction** — 69% of 53 data points cite it [K]. But it's a COMPOUND problem, not a simple "marketing" problem:

| Sub-friction | Frequency | Our tool solves? |
|---|---|---|
| Cold-start (first 10 users) | 68% | YES — channel ranking |
| Audience specificity gap | 64% | YES — AI product analysis |
| Channel paralysis (too many options) | 58% | YES — ranked list |
| Persistence gap (months 3-18) | 40% | PARTIAL — scripts reduce friction |
| Resource constraint (time+budget) | 35% | YES — instant results |

**Counter-evidence (22%):** PMF failures where distribution help is useless. Our tool should detect "your product has no clear audience" and say so instead of giving false hope.

